Vikram and Betal: The Lazy Man

King Vikram was once again carrying Betal through the forest.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a lazy man who did not like to work,” said Betal. “He always looked for easy ways to earn money.”

One day, he heard that the king rewards hardworking people.

So he went to the court and said, “Your Majesty, I work very hard. Please reward me.”

The king was unsure and asked, “What work do you do?”

The man had no answer.

Tenali Rama was present in the court and understood the situation.

He said, “Your Majesty, let us test him.”

Tenali gave the man a small task and said, “Complete this by tomorrow.”

The man did not do any work and returned empty-handed.

Tenali smiled and said, “This proves he is lazy.”

The king understood the truth and sent the man away.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what is the lesson here?”

Vikram replied, “Only those who work hard deserve rewards.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Hard work always brings rewards.
